course: dictionary
lesson: 526
title: Astrology: a belief, not a science
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound scientific but mean something different. Read the context to find out what kind of word it is. «Astrology says the stars at your birth shape your personality, but careful studies have found no good evidence for it.» The word but is a clue: the sentence is saying that astrology is a belief, and that the evidence does not back it up.
explain: Astrology and astronomy look alike, so check the clues carefully. «Astronomy is the science of space; astrology is a belief about stars and personality, and tests haven't shown it predicts anything.» The semicolon separates two ideas. Astronomy is the science. Astrology is the belief. The clue is in the words science and belief.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a fact that can be tested, or a belief? Scientists test ideas, and a good idea must match what happens. Tests haven't shown that astrology predicts anything, so people should not treat it as a science.
fact: «Astrology» means the belief that the Sun, Moon, planets and stars at the time someone is born affect their character and what happens to them.
fact: Astrology also means making horoscopes based on star signs, such as Aries, Leo or Capricorn.
fact: «Astronomy» is the science of space. Astrology is not the same thing.
fact: There is no good scientific evidence that astrology works, so many scientists and Christians do not accept it.
fact: People often read horoscopes in magazines for fun. Reading one for fun is different from believing it is science.
exercise: «Astrology says the stars at your birth shape your personality, but careful studies have found no good evidence for it.» What does astrology say? | Scientists have proved that astrology is true | *The stars at your birth shape your personality | Planets only move in circles | Stars are made of gas and burn very hot
exercise: Which word is the science of space? | Zodiac | *Astronomy | Astrology | Horoscope
exercise: What is a horoscope based on? | The weather on your birthday | *Star signs, such as Aries or Leo | The number of books you have read | Your favourite colour
test: «Tests haven't shown it predicts anything.» What does this tell you about astrology? | Scientists agree it is true | It always predicts the future | *It has not been shown to predict anything | It is the same thing as astronomy
test: Which phrase means the sign, such as Leo or Libra, that people read about in a horoscope? | Planet | Galaxy | *Star sign | Comet
exam: Mia reads her horoscope for fun and says it is proven science. What is the best reply? | Horoscopes are proven by every scientist | Astrology is a belief with no good scientific evidence, so it is not science, even if reading it is fun | *Wrong, astrology is astronomy, so it is science | Astrology is a fact about the Sun and the Moon only
